For each fixed finite set of sites, step 2.1 gives locally uniform convergence of its one-point and two-point expectations under $
u_{n,\lambda}$ to those under $\mu_\lambda$, hence locally uniform convergence of each covariance. For $i
e j$ in $\Lambda_n$, steps 1.2 and 3.1 give $|\operatorname{Cov}_{
u_{n,\lambda}}(\sigma_i,\sigma_j)|\leq\sum_{k\geq1}C(\lambda)^k_{ij}$; the diagonal variance is at most $1$. The same path-tail argument as in step 4.1 therefore bounds, uniformly in $n$ and $\lambda$, the sum of absolute covariances over sites outside any fixed box by a quantity tending to zero as the box grows. Splitting the covariance sum into that finite box and its uniformly small complement proves that the finite sums $S_n(\lambda):=\sum_{j\in\Lambda_n}\operatorname{Cov}_{
u_{n,\lambda}}(\sigma_0,\sigma_j)$ converge locally uniformly on $I$ to $S(\lambda):=\sum_{j\in\mathbb Z^d}\operatorname{Cov}_{\mu_\lambda}(\sigma_0,\sigma_j)$.

For $m_n(\lambda):=\mathbb E_{
