u_{n,\lambda}}(\sigma_0,\sigma_j)=S_n(\lambda)$. For the aggregate finite-volume identity, [F5] gives $d(\log Z)/dt= eta\mathbb E_tM_n$ and $d^2(\log Z)/dt^2= eta^2\operatorname{Var}_t(M_n)$. Since $t=\lambda/ eta$, the chain rule gives $d^2(\log Z)/d\lambda^2=\operatorname{Var}_{
